# DIRA LEARN - website build settings (21 Nov 2026 release). These two are PUBLIC values: they end up in the browser.
# Online: set them in Cloudflare (Workers & Pages > dira-learn-v2 > Settings > Build > Variables and secrets), using the NEW
# Supabase project's values from Project Settings > API (Project URL, and the anon or publishable key).
# Local checks only: copy to .env.local. Never commit real values.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=replace-with-local-anon-key-from-supabase-start

# Optional: address of the public DIRA Foundation website (used for the privacy and terms links and the cover photos).
# VITE_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://dirafoundationken.netlify.app

# NEVER here, in frontend code, in Cloudflare build variables or in the repository: the service-role key, the database
# password, SMTP/Resend passwords, Cloudflare API tokens, the setup code. Server-side secrets are set in the Supabase
# Dashboard (Edge Functions > Secrets) - see INSTALL_GUIDE.md part C:
#   SETUP_CODE         one-time code for the first Super Administrator (>= 20 characters); REMOVE it after setup
#   FIRST_ADMIN_EMAIL  marksmedia.studios@gmail.com (the only account the setup can create)
#   APP_URL            the website address, e.g. https://dira-learn-v2.<your-subdomain>.workers.dev
#   ALLOWED_ORIGINS    optional, extra website addresses (comma-separated)
#   CRON_SECRET, RESEND_API_KEY, EMAIL_FROM, RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRET   email (optional, docs/EMAIL_SETUP.md)
#   SCANNER_PROVIDER, SCANNER_URL                                    file scanning (optional, docs/ATTACHMENT_SECURITY.md)
# SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY are provided to Edge Functions by Supabase automatically.
